# Crypto primitive conventions

- Use `Uint8Array` for all binary data. Never use `Buffer` in public APIs.
- Prefer `crypto.getRandomValues` for IVs and symmetric keys; use Noble only where required.
- Throw descriptive `Error` messages for invalid inputs — include expected vs actual sizes.
- Provider implementations implement `PqcProvider`; primitives remain usable without a provider.
- New algorithms require a registry entry in `ENCLAVE_PQ_SUITE_v1.json` before code lands.

```typescript
// BAD — hardcoded algorithm id
const algo = "ML-KEM-768";

// GOOD — from registry
import { ML_KEM_ALGORITHM } from "../registry/suite.js";
```
